// Add to ~/.config/Antigravity/User/keybindings.json
// (VS Code: ~/.config/Code/User/keybindings.json)
//
// Opens the document manifest in the IDE's Simple Browser.
//
// Two phases via runCommands, deliberately:
//   1. "Ensure doc server" runs .claude/open-manifest.sh, which health-checks
//      the port and starts server.py if nothing is listening. Without this,
//      pressing Alt+D before the folderOpen auto-start task has bound (or after
//      the server died) shows connection-refused.
//   2. simpleBrowser.show opens the MANIFEST — the stable entry point listing
//      every document by date, so this URL never needs updating per document.
//
// It must be the simpleBrowser.show COMMAND, not a vscode:// URI: Antigravity
// ships the simple-browser extension but registers no
// vscode://vscode.simpleBrowser/show URI handler.
//
// The port below is only the default. open-manifest.sh rewrites this URL to
// match .claude/server.port, so a server that scanned past a busy 7432 does not
// leave the binding pointing at a dead port.
[
  {
    "key": "alt+d",
    "command": "runCommands",
    "args": {
      "commands": [
        { "command": "workbench.action.tasks.runTask", "args": "Ensure doc server" },
        { "command": "simpleBrowser.show", "args": "http://localhost:7432/manifest.html" }
      ]
    }
  }
]
